1
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:21,000
His past was kept from him, his search for answers has just begun.

2
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:36,000
The Amazing Spider-Man is a action, adventure, science
fiction film directed by Marc Webb.

3
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:51,000
Peter Parker is an outcast high schooler abandoned by his parents as a
boy, leaving him to be raised by his Uncle Ben and Aunt May.

4
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:06,000
Like most teenagers, Peter is trying to figure out who he is
and how he got to be the person he is today.

5
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:21,000
As Peter discovers a mysterious briefcase that belonged to his father, he begins a quest to
understand his parents' disappearance – leading him directly to Oscorp and the lab of Dr.

6
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:36,000
Curt Connors, his father's former partner.

7
00:29:45,000 --> 00:29:51,000
As Spider-Man is set on a collision course with Connors' alter ego, The Lizard, Peter will make
life-altering choices to use his powers and shape his destiny to become a hero.

8
00:34:00,000 --> 00:34:06,000
Spider-Man / Peter Parker, played by Andrew Garfield.

9
00:38:15,000 --> 00:38:21,000
Gwen Stacy, played by Emma Stone.

10
00:42:30,000 --> 00:42:36,000
The Lizard / Dr. Curt Connors, played by Rhys Ifans.

11
00:46:45,000 --> 00:46:51,000
Captain Stacy, played by Denis Leary.

12
00:51:00,000 --> 00:51:06,000
Uncle Ben, played by Martin Sheen.

13
00:55:15,000 --> 00:55:21,000
Aunt May, played by Sally Field.

14
00:59:30,000 --> 00:59:36,000
The Amazing Spider-Man is a 2012 American superhero film
based on the Marvel Comics character Spider-Man.

15
01:03:45,000 --> 01:03:51,000
Directed by Marc Webb and written by James Vanderbilt, Alvin Sargent, and Steve Kloves
from a story by Vanderbilt, it is a reboot of the Spider-Man film series.

16
01:08:00,000 --> 01:08:06,000
Andrew Garfield stars as Peter Parker / Spider-Man alongside Emma Stone, Rhys Ifans,
Denis Leary, Campbell Scott, Irrfan Khan, Martin Sheen, and Sally Field.

17
01:12:15,000 --> 01:12:21,000
The plot of the film follows the teenager Peter Parker, who gains spider-like abilities and
fights crime as Spider-Man, while also attempting to live an ordinary life.

18
01:16:30,000 --> 01:16:36,000
Development of the film began in 2010 following the cancellation of Spider-Man 4, which would
have been the fourth film in Sam Raimi's Spider-Man series starring Tobey Maguire.

19
01:20:45,000 --> 01:20:51,000
Columbia Pictures opted to reboot the franchise with the same production team, with
Vanderbilt staying on to write, and Sargent and Kloves assisting with the script.

20
01:25:00,000 --> 01:25:06,000
Using the RED Epic camera, principal photography started in December
2010 in Los Angeles before moving to New York City.

21
01:29:15,000 --> 01:29:21,000
The film entered post-production in April 2011.

22
01:33:30,000 --> 01:33:36,000
3ality Technica provided 3D image processing, while Sony
Pictures Imageworks handled CGI effects.

23
01:37:45,000 --> 01:37:51,000
It was the last film written by Sargent before his death in 2019.

24
01:42:00,000 --> 01:42:06,000
Sony Pictures Entertainment built a promotional website, releasing many previews and launching a
viral marketing campaign, with tie-ins including a video game by Beenox and Activision.

25
01:46:15,000 --> 01:46:21,000
The Amazing Spider-Man premiered in Tokyo on June 30, 2012, and was released in
2D, 3D, IMAX 3D, and 4DX formats in the United States on July 3.

26
01:50:30,000 --> 01:50:36,000
It received mostly positive reviews from critics, who praised the directing, action
sequences, visual effects, musical score, and the performances of Garfield and Stone.

27
01:54:45,000 --> 01:54:51,000
The film grossed $758.7 million worldwide, making it the
seventh-highest-grossing film of 2012.

28
01:59:00,000 --> 01:59:06,000
A sequel, The Amazing Spider-Man 2, was released in 2014.

29
02:03:15,000 --> 02:03:21,000
In 2021, Garfield and Ifans reprised their roles in the Marvel Cinematic Universe film Spider-Man: No Way Home, which explored the
concept of the multiverse and linked the Spider-Man series directed by Jon Watts to the films directed by Webb and Raimi.

30
02:07:30,000 --> 02:07:36,000
The film explores themes of experiment, loss of loved
one, superhero, based on comic, vigilante.

31
02:11:45,000 --> 02:11:51,000
The tone is thought_provoking.
